  "reason": "Evidence: Our only completed experiment (config_015) achieved ~52% accuracy with multimodal/multiprofile/scgpt/imagenet_vit_l/transformer/weighted. This is a single data point, so we have high uncertainty about which components are driving performance. Question: config_012 is a single-variable change from config_015, swapping imagenet_vit_l for resnet50 while keeping all other settings identical (scgpt, transformer, weighted, multiprofile). This directly tests whether the stronger image encoder (ViT-L) is a critical contributor or whether a simpler CNN (ResNet50) suffices. Why this is the best next experiment: The image encoder is a high-impact architectural choice that appears in many of the remaining untested configurations. Resolving whether imagenet_vit_l is necessary will (a) confirm or eliminate a key design constraint for the remaining 8 experiments, and (b) if resnet50 performs comparably, free us to explore other dimensions (aggregation, fusion, RNA encoder) without the heavier ViT-L. This clean A/B test maximizes information gain per experiment under our tight budget."
}

